 ## Overview
-Backbone Fine-tuning adapts the weights of a pre-trained 3D generator (backbone) alongside the decoder to generate Gaussian Splatting attributes, addressing the fact that splats have scale and rotation that influence adjacent regions, unlike NeRF's local color/density [S1]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Exponentially Ascending Gradient Threshold](9684-exponentially-ascending-gradient-threshold.md) by modifying the generative prior itself rather than just the optimization trajectory, and from [Dual-branch Architecture for Attribute Learning](#dual-branch-architecture-for-attribute-learning) by potentially updating geometry if not explicitly frozen [S1][S2, unofficial].
